## Begin with artwork that suits the object

A pin, coin, medal, keychain, or plaque has its own scale and functional limits. Artwork review resolves the silhouette, dimensions, relief, lettering, color areas, front and reverse, and any edge or attachment requirements before tooling begins.

## Form and finish the metal

Depending on the product, the process can involve molding, tooling, stamping, die casting, polishing, enameling, printing, and plating. Each stage changes how the design looks and feels, so finish choices should be made with the actual object in mind.

## Assemble, inspect, and pack

Backings, rings, chains, ribbons, leather elements, and other fittings complete the piece. Quality checks continue from materials through assembly and final packing so the approved design and order specification stay aligned.
